  "description": "Na₃CoO₃ crystallizes in the cubic I̅43m space group. Na is bonded to five equivalent O atoms to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing NaO₅ square pyramids. There are a spread of Na-O bond distances ranging from 2.37-2.50 Å. Co is bonded in a trigonal planar geometry to three equivalent O atoms. All Co-O bond lengths are 1.79 Å. O is bonded to five equivalent Na and one Co atom to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing ONa₅Co octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles are 17°.",
